    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0132" n="87" xml:id="pg87"/>

                <head>27. Telegram From the Embassy in Bangladesh to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d27-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Dacca</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1977-10-02T00:18:00+00:00">October 2, 1977,
                        0018Z</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5583. Subject: Hijacking and Internal Security in Dacca.</p>
                <p>Control tower has reported to hijackers “a serious development” which has nothing
                    to do with the hijacking. The tower advised the hijackers that “unruly uniformed
                    people who are armed” may approach the aircraft. If this happens, the tower
                    stated, the hijackers should take “full defensive positions and after checking
                    with the tower as to identity of the people, be prepared to shoot them” to
                    protect the passengers and crew.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Masters</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d27-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d27-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Foreign
                    Policy File, D770382–0854, D770359–0634. Confidential; Immediate. Sent for
                    information Immediate to Tokyo. Sent for information to DIA.</p>
            </note>
